Description: A crop on each eye takes its amounts in the clip's own samples; two more services are told
 A service set up on one eye of a frame of two eyes (its process) was told one
 eye's size as half the frame of two eyes. Crop sizes itself then: with "Use
 Project Resolution" off its amounts are the clip's own samples, so on a clip
 whose views are not of the project's shape (4:3 views in a 16:9 project, half
 views) each eye was cut by amounts read as samples of the project's eye, not
 as a 2D project of that eye cuts it. stereo3d_unpack now says each view's own
 size on the frame and the framework tells the service that size, and back to
 the frame of two eyes when it leaves. Views of the project's shape do not
 change (their size is half the frame).
 .
 frei0r.vertigo and frei0r.timeout were marked as services for which the frame
 of two eyes as a whole gives what each eye apart gives. Measured, it does
 not: vertigo keeps earlier pictures and draws them again turned and zoomed,
 across the middle; timeout draws its timer once, in one eye. They are now of
 the kind that acts on the two eyes as one picture, which Kdenlive's effect
 panel tells the person.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Forwarded: not-yet
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
